Ang objective natin:

Router = DHCP Server + Inter-VLAN Routing
Core Switch = Layer 2 aggregation/trunking only
Access Switches = VLAN + port assignment + trunking

So essentially, aalisin natin ang SVI/gateway function sa CoreSwitch at ililipat sa Router-on-a-Stick.

                 ┌───────────────────┐
                 │       ROUTER      │
                 │                   │
                 │ DHCP SERVER       │
                 │ Inter-VLAN Routing│
                 │                   │
                 │ G0/0              │
                 └─────────┬─────────┘
                           │
                        TRUNK
                           │
                 ┌─────────┴─────────┐
                 │    CORE SWITCH    │
                 │                   │
                 │ L2 ONLY           │
                 │ NO SVI GATEWAYS   │
                 │ TRUNKING ONLY     │
                 └─────┬─────┬───────┘
                       │     │
                    TRUNK   TRUNK
                       │     │
                 ┌─────┘     └─────┐
                 │                 │
          ACCESS SWITCH 1     ACCESS SWITCH 2
          VLANs/Ports         VLANs/Ports

At yung telephony router mo puwede pa ring manatili sa topology. Hindi natin kailangang galawin muna iyon.

Habang ginagawa mo, ito lang ang mental checklist mo:

Sino ang gateway ng bawat VLAN?
Dati: CoreSwitch SVI
Ngayon: Router subinterface
Sino ang DHCP server?
Dati: CoreSwitch
Ngayon: 2811 Router
Ano ang role ng CoreSwitch?
L2 switching
VLANs
Trunking
Hindi na siya ang nag-i-inter-VLAN routing
Paano makakarating ang multiple VLANs sa isang router interface?
Router-on-a-Stick
802.1Q
Subinterfaces
Ano ang mananatiling pareho?
VLAN IDs
Access-port assignments
Access-switch configuration
Trunk concept

!assign a designated native vlan for trunking
1. Create muna ang VLAN 100
conf t
vlan 100
 name NATIVE_VLAN
exit

2. Sa trunk port
Halimbawa Gi0/1 ang trunk:
interface gi0/1
 switchport mode trunk
 switchport trunk native vlan 100
exit

!!router configurations for DHCP and SVI
interface fa0/0.40 !!<- meaning port#.vlanID
 encapsulation dot1Q 40
 ip address 192.168.40.1 255.255.255.0 !!<-- default gateway of VLAN ID

!!4. At dito papasok ang DHCP
Sa router:
ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.40.1 192.168.40.10
!!Then:
ip dhcp pool SALES
 network 192.168.40.0 255.255.255.0
 default-router 192.168.40.1
 dns-server 8.8.8.8

!5. Pero may isang critical detail: Native VLAN 100
!Since ginawa natin:

switchport trunk native vlan 100

!!ang router side ay kailangan ding magkaroon ng native VLAN subinterface kung gusto nating explicitly handle ang VLAN 100.
!For example:

interface fa0/0.100
encapsulation dot1Q 100 native

!!Pero hindi natin kailangang lagyan ng IP kung dedicated/unused native VLAN lang siya.

!!So:

interface fa0/0.100
 encapsulation dot1Q 100 native

!Then:
!Switch                         Router
!Native VLAN 100  <----------> Fa0/0.100
!VLAN 40          <----------> Fa0/0.40
!VLAN 50          <----------> Fa0/0.50
!VLAN 60          <----------> Fa0/0.60

!!6. Very important: hindi switchport trunk ang router
!!Ito ang common mistake kapag unang beses nag-ROAS.
!!Switch:

interface gi1/0/24
 switchport mode trunk
 switchport trunk native vlan 100
 switchport trunk allowed vlan 10-70,99-100

!!Router:

interface fa0/0
 no shutdown

!!Then subinterfaces:

interface fa0/0.40
 encapsulation dot1Q 40
 ip address 192.168.40.1 255.255.255.0
